ermediate"><addressbook><name>KAWASE, RITSU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOBAYASHI, TATSUSHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SASAKI, KYOICHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUKEGAWA, KEN</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TOMOEGAWA PAPER CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KAWASE RITSU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KOBAYASHI TATSUSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SASAKI KYOICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SUKEGAWA KEN</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KAWASE, RITSU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOBAYASHI, TATSUSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SASAKI, KYOICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUKEGAWA, KEN</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An optical connecting component which does not disturb the arrangement pattern of optical fibers, protects the optical fibers against an external force, simplifies the optical connection, and improves the environmental resistance and reliability. An adhesive layer (3) is provided in a base (1) or a resin protective layer. Optical fibers (4) having an optical connector at their ends are arranged two-dimensionally on the adhesive layer (3) and fixed with the resin protective layer (2). The resin protective layer (2) is made of a silicone material which cured with the progress of condensation reaction by deoximation or dealcoholization or of a mixture of a silicone material crosslinked and cured by hydrosilylation reaction and an adhesion-imparting agent. The adhesive layer (3) is made of an acrylic pressure-sensitive adhesive or a silicone pressure-sensitive adhesive crosslinked and cured by hydrosilylation reaction.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un composant de connexion optique, qui ne perturbe pas la configuration des fibres optiques, qui protège les fibres optiques d'une force externe, et qui améliore leur résistance au milieu environnant et leur fiabilité. A cet effet, on applique une couche adhésive (3) sur une base (1) ou sur une couche de protection en résine. On dispose des fibres optiques (4) pourvues d'un connecteur optique à leurs extrémités dans les deux dimensions sur la couche adhésive (3) et on les fixe à l'aide de la couche (2) de protection en résine. Cette couche (2) de protection en résine est constituée d'un matériau de silicone qui durcit au cours d'une réaction de condensation par déoxymation ou désalcoolisation d'un mélange constitué d'un matériau de silicone réticulé et durci par réaction d'hydrosilylation et d'un agent conférant de l'adhérence. La couche adhésive (3) est constituée d'un adhésif acrylique sensible à la pression ou d'un adhésif de silicone sensible à la pression réticulé et durci par réaction d'hydrosilylation.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>